\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-270\li270\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. \cf0  The Virgin Mary with her child
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0 came up to the Temple,
\par and Simeon the Old wise man
\par saw Him a comforter.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-270\li270\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2.  He took Him on his arms and said:
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 Blessed be to the Lord.
\par He said:  Now I have found my peace;
\par and I can leave for home.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3.  O Jesus Christ, the Son of God,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 give unto us the joy
\par that Simeon had once received,
\par and give to us your peace.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4.  And when the day of toil is done
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 Let me sing to your praise
\par That: I have seen my Saviour Lord,
\par \pard      Eternity I come.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2 
\par }

